WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.628
"Hello and welcome to the Little Fox Animal Report.

2
00:00:06.629 --> 00:00:13.379
I am your host, Ian Shelback. Tonight, I am in Forest, Canada.

3
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:18.931
I am interviewing a very special red fox named Boxer.

4
00:00:18.932 --> 00:00:23.204
He is the oldest fox in this forest.

5
00:00:23.205 --> 00:00:25.368
Good evening, Boxer."

6
00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:27.605
"Good evening, Ian."

7
00:00:27.606 --> 00:00:31.134
"Boxer, can you tell us about your life?

8
00:00:31.135 --> 00:00:34.713
What's life like here in the Canadian forest?"

9
00:00:34.714 --> 00:00:41.141
"Well, Ian, I would be delighted to tell you about my life.

10
00:00:41.142 --> 00:00:43.411
Where should I begin?

11
00:00:43.412 --> 00:00:50.701
Let me tell you about how I met my darling wife, Bridget.

12
00:00:50.702 --> 00:00:58.685
When I was a young fox, I left my family. I wanted to see the world.

13
00:00:58.686 --> 00:01:02.111
'Good luck, Boxer. Take care.'

14
00:01:02.112 --> 00:01:11.319
'Good-bye, Mother. Good-bye, Father. Good-bye, Family.'

15
00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.487
I traveled for almost one month.

16
00:01:14.488 --> 00:01:20.406
It was late summer so the forest was green and full of small animals.

17
00:01:20.407 --> 00:01:24.727
I especially liked to catch rabbits and birds.

18
00:01:24.728 --> 00:01:34.786
One day, while I was chasing a squirrel through a meadow, I met the prettiest vixen I have ever seen.

19
00:01:34.787 --> 00:01:43.286
Her face and ears were wonderfully pointed; her fur was long and her tail was very bushy.

20
00:01:43.287 --> 00:01:50.897
I don't think she weighed more than 3.6 kilograms. She was very slim.

21
00:01:50.898 --> 00:01:55.650
'Hello, I'm Bridget. I have never seen you before.'

22
00:01:55.651 --> 00:02:02.792
'Well hello, I'm Boxer. I am from very far away.

23
00:02:02.793 --> 00:02:07.276
I have been traveling through the forest.'

24
00:02:07.277 --> 00:02:13.371
'Traveling! That sounds exciting! I have lived here all my life.

25
00:02:13.372 --> 00:02:17.608
I would like to . . . AHH!'

26
00:02:17.609 --> 00:02:25.626
Just then, a large wolf jumped out from behind a tree and tried to make us his supper.

27
00:02:25.627 --> 00:02:32.365
As quick as I could, I grabbed Bridget and we ran into a small hole.

28
00:02:32.366 --> 00:02:42.496
We barely escaped. From that day forward, we fell in love and lived happily together."

29
00:02:42.497 --> 00:02:45.949
"Did you build a house for your wife?"

30
00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:50.953
"Ian, red foxes don't like to have permanent houses.

31
00:02:50.954 --> 00:02:54.367
We usually spend our time outside.

32
00:02:54.368 --> 00:03:02.391
Even in the winter, when the other animals are hibernating, we play outside in the snow.

33
00:03:02.392 --> 00:03:07.645
By late December, it was time for us to start our family.

34
00:03:07.646 --> 00:03:13.487
I searched and searched for the best place to build a den.

35
00:03:13.488 --> 00:03:18.386
A den needs to be warm and dry for the cubs.

36
00:03:18.387 --> 00:03:24.814
'Boxer, we must find a den soon. Our cubs will come very soon.'

37
00:03:24.815 --> 00:03:30.464
'Don't worry, Bridget. I have found a great place for a den.

38
00:03:30.465 --> 00:03:37.143
It is an old groundhog's den. It is not too far away.'

39
00:03:37.144 --> 00:03:44.615
That very night, after we had settled into our new den, our cubs were born.

40
00:03:44.616 --> 00:03:55.047
We had six wonderful young cubs, three boys and three girls. It was terrific."

41
00:03:55.048 --> 00:03:58.908
"What was it like taking care of six young cubs?

42
00:03:58.909 --> 00:04:01.456
It must have been very hard work."

43
00:04:01.457 --> 00:04:04.232
"Well, it certainly was.

44
00:04:04.233 --> 00:04:11.254
You know, when they are born they cannot even see for nine days.

45
00:04:11.255 --> 00:04:16.132
Over the next two months the cubs grew and grew.

46
00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:20.774
Soon they were ready for their hunting lessons.

47
00:04:20.775 --> 00:04:27.085
'Okay, Children. Today you are going to get your first hunting lesson.

48
00:04:27.086 --> 00:04:34.552
Usually, we like to hunt these animals: rabbits, squirrels, and mice.

49
00:04:34.553 --> 00:04:38.362
Today, we will practice catching mice.

50
00:04:38.363 --> 00:04:44.854
Mice are not easy to catch so you will have to pay close attention.'

51
00:04:44.855 --> 00:04:51.429
After six months, Bridget and I had to say good-bye to our cubs.

52
00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:56.659
They were ready to go out into the world on their own.

53
00:04:56.660 --> 00:05:03.042
'Good-bye, my lovely cubs. Take care. Watch out for wolves!'

54
00:05:03.043 --> 00:05:07.091
'Good-bye, Mother; good-bye, Father.'

55
00:05:07.092 --> 00:05:10.593
'Good-bye, Children.'

56
00:05:10.594 --> 00:05:17.485
Bridget and I lived many happy years together and had many more wonderful cubs.

57
00:05:17.486 --> 00:05:22.037
My life has been great."

58
00:05:22.038 --> 00:05:26.956
"Well, thank you, Boxer. It has been great talking to you."

59
00:05:26.957 --> 00:05:38.157
"Before I go, I would like to say that I know that some people think foxes are mean and cunning, but we are not.

60
00:05:38.158 --> 00:05:42.122
We are kind and gentle."

61
00:05:42.123 --> 00:05:44.276
"Of course you are.

62
00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:46.896
That was Boxer the fox.

63
00:05:46.897 --> 00:05:54.149
This has been Ian Shelback for the Little Fox Animal Report in Forest, Canada.

64
00:05:54.150 --> 00:06:02.045
Thank you for joining us and see you next time when we interview another interesting forest animal."

